    {
      "id": "efe17b50-2bb4-460f-bfc0-783628862fa6",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## Push Git\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow is triggered by another n8n workflow and receives or normalizes a workflow ID. It fetches that workflow from n8n, keeps only the properties needed for version control, converts the result into a JSON file, then checks GitHub for the corresponding file. Depending on whether the file exists and has changes, it either creates a new GitHub file or updates the existing one.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the n8n credentials/permissions so the workflow can read workflows by ID.\n- Configure the GitHub credentials on the GitHub nodes with access to the target repository and branch.\n- Set the expected workflow ID input used by the trigger and confirm the file path/name conventions in the GitHub create, read, and edit nodes.\n- Verify the filtered workflow properties match what should be committed to Git.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the filtered fields, JSON file naming/path, target repository/branch, and the modification condition to change what gets pushed and when."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a6ec05ed-c661-455c-b6f7-d0cfbc604bdd",
